      "message": "feat(xtask): the heavy reach of a library file follows the Gate maps\n\nA changed library module of crate d now reaches the lib, bins and doc\ntargets of d and the heavy binaries whose Gate map names the module. The\nquick plan uses the same seam. The module names and the match rule move\nout of quick::map_modules into quick::src_modules, quick::gate_maps and\nquick::suites_naming, so the two plans share one rule.\n\nThe crate reach stays for a shared crate, a crate root, a file outside\nsrc/, and a file that no Gate map names.\n\nExample: crates/motion/src/drilling/boss.rs goes from 115 heavy steps\nto 11.\n\nFixes #3560\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
